CODE Explaination:

1)Header file:
1.stdio.h, 2.stdlib.h, 3.conio.h, 4.windows.h, 5.time.h
What they do do:
1.Input and output: printf(), fopen(), fscanf()
2.General functions: rand(), srand()
3.Keyboard input: _getch(), _kbhit()
4.Windows functions: Sleep()
5.Gets current time: time()

For example:
. stdio.h prints the score.
. stdlib.h generates random obstacle positions.
. conio.h allows us to detect when the player presses A or D.
. windows.h pauses the game for a short time.
. time.h generates random numbers every time the game starts.

2)Function Declaration

3)Main function
.Main Variables: 
road[][]     : it stores the road as 12 rows and 3 lanes
car=1        : puts your car in the middle lane
obs          : which lane the obstacle is in
obsrow=0     : decides which lane the obstacle apears in
score=0      : stores current score
highscore=0  : stores highscore
i, j         : used for loops
FILE *file   : file handling

.Columns of array:
column 0 = left lane 
column 1 = middle lane
column 2 = right lane

.Number Generation:
1.srand(time(0)); : initializes the random number generator and gets current time (makes random sequence different when you run the code again)
2.obstacle = rand() % 3; : generates a random number, the "% 3" takes the remainder after divind it by 3, resulting 0, 1 or 2 making the obstacle apear in the three columns

.highscore:
1.file = fopen("highscore.txt", "r"); : reads the highscore
2.if (file != NULL){ : checks if the file exists and opens
3.fscanf(file, "%d", &highscore) : reads the number stored in the file and put it in highscore

.menu:
printf("**** ROAD RUNNER ****\n");
printf("High Score: %d\n", highscore);
printf("A = Left | D = Right | Q = Quit\n");
printf("Press any key to start...");
_getch(); : waits for user to press a key, scanf requires user to press Enter

.loop:
1.while(1) : the loop keeps running infinitely. helps check keyboard input, update road, move obstacle, check collisions, update score
2. break stops the loop

.keyboard input:
 if (_kbhit()) {
     char key = _getch();
1. _kbhit() : checks if a key has been pressed. 1 if pressed, 0 if no key pressed
2. char key = _getch() : reads the key pressed and stores it in "key"
3.condition:  if (key == 'a' && car > 0) {
    car--;
}
This condition checks if user pressed a and is the car's position greater than 0 (0 is the last lane, car cant move further left)
car-- : makes the car position go to column 0

Same conditions apply for "d" but if car goes to right lane and "q" is to quit the game.

.Clearing the Road:
for (i = 0; i < 12; i++) {
    for (j = 0; j < 3; j++) {
        road[i][j] = ' ';
    }
}
-first loop is for 12 rows for the road to be long
-second loop is for 3 lanes for the car and obstacles to appear in the 3 lanes only
-road[i][j] = ' '; : places empty space every row


.Placing obstacles and car on road:
road[obsrow][obs] = 'X'; :puts obstacles on the road
road[11][car] = 'A' : puts car in the last row 11th row as array starts from 0 so 12th row is 11th 

.Displaying road:
droad(road, score); : sends the road array and current score

.Collision:
if (obsrow == 11 && car == obstacle) {
    break;
}
game ends if obstacle and car on the same row

.obsrow++ : moves the obstacle's row by 1
if (obsrow == 12) { 
    obsrow = 0;
    obs = rand() % 3;
    score += 10;
}
This part of code tells us if the obstacle reaches row 12, move it to row 0
obs = rand() %3; : chooses a new random lane  
score+= 10; : increases the users score by 10

.Sleep(150) : pauses the game for 150 milliseconds or else the game would run very fast

.system("cls"); : clears the terminal screen

.After collsion menu:
printf("GAME OVER!\n");
printf("Your Score: %d\n", score);

.Checking and displaying highscore:
if (score > highscore) {
    printf("NEW HIGH SCORE!\n");
    savescore(score);
}
else {
    printf("High Score: %d\n", highscore);
}


.Exit menu:
printf("\nPress any key to exit...");
_getch();
return 0;
}


.droad() function:
1.system("cls"); : closes terminal before the updated row
2.printf("ROAD RUNNER\n");
printf("Score: %d\n", score);
printf("-------------------\n"); : Displays the game score
3.for (i = 0; i < 12; i++) {  :goes through 12 rows
    printf("|");              :prints left boundary
    for (j = 0; j < 3; j++) { :goes through 3 lanes
    printf(" %c |", road[i][j]); :displays char stored in that position (a,d or obstacle)
    }
    printf("\n");             :moves to next line
}

.savescore() function:
1.FILE *file; :creates a file pointer
2.file = fopen("highscore.txt", "w"); : wrties over previous content
3.if (file != NULL) { :checks if file opened and exists
4.fprintf(file, "%d", score); :writes user score in file
5.fclose(file); :closes file
